{"retractions" [[17592186347614 :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}},\\,0\\le y\\le 2z}.\n$$"] [17592186347614 :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{2z}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}[y]_{y=0}^{y=2z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}2z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{[{z}^{2}]}_{z=-0}^{z=\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{(\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}})}^{2}-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}2-{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[2x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=-2}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(2(2)-\\frac{1}{3}(2)^{3})-(2(-2)-\\frac{1}{3}(-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =(4-\\frac{8}{3})-(-4+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186347614 :question/answer-fields 17592186347615]] "immutable_answers" [17592186347616 17592186347617 17592186347618 17592186347619 17592186347620] "immutable_fields" [[17592186347615 :answer-field/id] [17592186347615 :answer-field/key] [17592186347615 :answer-field/type] [17592186347615 :answer-field/correct] [17592186347615 :answer-field/choices]]}
